Copyright (c) 2026 Guillermo Llopis-Garcia (SOMA, somaai.earth). All rights not expressly granted are reserved.

This licence applies to the SOMA AI Emission Factors (SAEF) dataset from version 3.3.0 onward, including every data file, table, factor, coefficient and documentation file in this release and every later release that names this licence, however obtained (Zenodo, Hugging Face, Kaggle, the `saef` Python package, the SOMA browser extension, the SOMA MCP server, the SOMA API, the SOMA websites or any copy of them). Earlier releases keep the licence they were published under.

## 1. Free use

You may use, copy and adapt the Data free of charge, with attribution (section 4), only for the following purposes ("Non-Commercial Use"):

a. **Personal use** by an individual, outside any trade, business, profession, employment or paid engagement;
b. **Academic and non-profit research and teaching**, where the results are published or made publicly available;
c. **Journalism and public-interest reporting** that is not itself a paid service to a client;
d. **Use by a non-commercial organisation**: a registered charity, a public or non-profit educational or research institution, or a government body, for its own non-commercial purposes.

## 2. Commercial use requires a paid licence

Every other use is "Commercial Use" and needs a separate written commercial licence from SOMA before it starts. For clarity, Commercial Use includes, without limitation:

a. any use by or on behalf of a company, partnership, for-profit organisation, sole trader or freelancer, **including internal use**, such as sustainability, ESG, CSRD, VSME, GHG-inventory or Scope 3 reporting, dashboards, procurement, budgeting, cost analysis or internal tools;
b. any use by an individual in the course of their employment or professional work for an organisation that is not covered by section 1(d);
c. providing services to clients, including consulting, auditing, assurance, reporting, measurement or advisory services that use the Data or results derived from it;
d. embedding, integrating or exposing the Data, or values derived from it, in a product, platform, application, API, plugin, model or service, whether paid or free of charge;
e. redistributing, selling, sublicensing or republishing the Data, or a substantial part of it, under any licence.

Using the factor values of a release covered by this licence counts as using the Data, whether they are read from SOMA's files, tools or API, or copied, typed or re-implemented in your own code, spreadsheets or systems.

Commercial licences: guillermollopis@somaai.earth, or see https://somaai.earth/licensing.

## 3. What this licence does not restrict

This licence does not restrict the use of ideas, methods or formulas described in SOMA's publications, which you may implement independently with your own data and your own values. It does not restrict quoting a small number of individual values in a review, publication or discussion with attribution.

## 4. Attribution

Any permitted use must cite: Llopis-Garcia, G. (2026). SOMA AI Emission Factors (SAEF), version X.Y.Z. Zenodo. https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20443585. Licensed under the SOMA AI Emission Factors Data Licence 1.0 (Non-Commercial).

## 5. Third-party data

Some values are derived from third-party sources that keep their own licences and attribution requirements, listed in `THIRD_PARTY_DATA.md` and `input_register.csv`. Nothing in this licence restricts what those licences allow for the original third-party data.

## 6. Termination

If you breach this licence, your rights under it end automatically. They are restored if you stop the breach, or obtain a commercial licence, within 30 days of written notice from SOMA, the first time only.

